    {
      "id": "Z-vzwXWy81YzC-AXj3Nfn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -41294.166687188124,
      "y": -6468.207039468903,
      "width": 1717.038818359375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 802084666,
      "version": 674,
      "versionNonce": 1380521190,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784135360800,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to ensure comments are broadcasted to viewers in real-time?\n- Polling doesn't gives us realtime\n\n1. Good Solution : Websockets\n- Pass on the comments in real time to all the connected viewers\n\nProblems\n- They are good for bi-directional like chat-application(balanced read/write ratio) but here server is only sending messages as comment creation is infrequent\n- Overhead of maintaining the connection is high, as there's a API gateway that has to actually mimic websocket connection i.e. client <-> gatewat <-> server both websockets\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to ensure comments are broadcasted to viewers in real-time?\n- Polling doesn't gives us realtime\n\n1. Good Solution : Websockets\n- Pass on the comments in real time to all the connected viewers\n\nProblems\n- They are good for bi-directional like chat-application(balanced read/write ratio) but here server is only sending messages as comment creation is infrequent\n- Overhead of maintaining the connection is high, as there's a API gateway that has to actually mimic websocket connection i.e. client <-> gatewat <-> server both websockets\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
